{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Sarek_launch_bounds</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"sarek","href":"../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Sarek_launch_bounds","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-directive\"><a href=\"#val-directive\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> directive : string</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-max_allowed\"><a href=\"#val-max_allowed\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> max_allowed : int</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Largest work-group size any supported backend accepts. A bound above it can never be met, so it is refused as a mistake rather than carried along.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-parsed\"><a href=\"#type-parsed\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> parsed</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-parsed.Not_a_launch_bound\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-parsed.Not_a_launch_bound\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Not_a_launch_bound</span></span></code></li><li id=\"type-parsed.Bound\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-parsed.Bound\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Bound</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> int</span></code></li><li id=\"type-parsed.Malformed\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-parsed.Malformed\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Malformed</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> string</span></code></li></ol></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-parse\"><a href=\"#val-parse\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> parse : <span><span>string list</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"#type-parsed\">parsed</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Classify pragma options. Both <code>[&quot;sarek.max_threads N&quot;]</code> and <code>[&quot;sarek.max_threads&quot;; &quot;N&quot;]</code> spellings are accepted, like <code>sarek.inline</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-peel\"><a href=\"#val-peel\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> peel : <span><a href=\"../Sarek_typed_ast/index.html#type-texpr\">Sarek_typed_ast.texpr</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span>int option</span> * <a href=\"../Sarek_typed_ast/index.html#type-texpr\">Sarek_typed_ast.texpr</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Strip the leading <code>sarek.max_threads</code> pragma(s) from a kernel body. Returns the bound (None when absent) and the remaining body. Two declarations on one kernel are refused.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-reject_misplaced\"><a href=\"#val-reject_misplaced\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> reject_misplaced : <span><span class=\"label\">loc</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ppxlib</span>.location <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span>string list</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Refuse <code>sarek.max_threads</code> anywhere but around the whole kernel body: a bound that no backend would see must not be silently accepted.</p></div></div>"}